{"metadata":{"description":"Lightweight requirement alignment for DeepSeek Harness — align important decisions before execution without a full spec workflow.","id":"gh:1334298839","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-requirements-alignment","slug":"jiezeng2004-design/dsh-requirements-alignment","topics":["agent","ai-agent","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","requirement-alignment"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Lightweight requirement alignment for DeepSeek Harness — align important decisions before execution "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"without a full spec workflow."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-requirements-alignment"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> **Stop long-running agents from quietly changing what you asked for.**
>
> 让 DSH Agent 自己做工程决策，但别让"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"它在长任务里悄悄改需求、扩范围、换架构。"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"`dsh-requirements-alignment` is a lightweight runtime drift guard for **DeepSeek Harness (DSH)**. It"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" turns the user's intent into a durable requirement baseline, stays out of the way while the agent w"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"orks, and only interrupts when the next step would materially change the direction."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**You decide the direction. The agent decides the engineering.**"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Current release candidate: **v0.5.0-rc.1**, targeting DeepSeek Harness **0.1.7-rc.2**. Requires Node"},{"id":"p6s2","text":".js **>=22.18.0**. See the compatibility report for verified behavior and limits."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## The problem"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Long-running coding agents are good at keeping momentum. That is also how they can drift."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"A task may start as:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Later the agent discovers that a cleaner solution would require backend changes. Without an explicit"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" guardrail, it may simply expand the scope and continue."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Requirements Alignment changes that behavior:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## What counts as drift"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The plugin is interested in **direction-level changes**, not implementation trivia."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Typical drift candidates include:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- expanding or shrinking the approved scope;
- violating an explicit constraint;
- changing user-vis"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ible behavior;
- switching architecture or product form;
- invalidating a settled assumption;
- chan"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ging a previously approved user decision;
- taking a destructive path that changes the intended outc"},{"id":"p17s4","text":" a previously approved user decision;
- taking a destructive path that changes the intended outcome."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"It should **not** stop the agent to ask about variable names, helper placement, ordinary refactors i"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"nside the approved scope, or other routine engineering choices."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Requirements Alignment vs Plan Mode"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Plan Mode helps before implementation starts. Requirements Alignment protects intent **during execut"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ode helps before implementation starts. Requirements Alignment protects intent **during execution**."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"They are complementary:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Install this release candidate into your DSH Web profile:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Then use DSH normally."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"**Auto mode is the recommended default.** Clear tasks continue with zero interruption. When a real d"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"irection change appears, the plugin surfaces one decision and records the result."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Use `/align` any time you want an explicit status check."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Three modes"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| Mode | Behavior |"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| **Auto** | Watches for direction-level drift and asks only when necessary |
| **Manual** | No auto"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"matic drift policy; use `/align` when you want a check |
| **Off** | Alignment capabilities are disa"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"bled for that session; `/align-mode` remains available so you can switch back |"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Common commands:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Per-session control:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"A session override changes only that session. Shared runtime settings remain separate. On DSH 0.1.7,"},{"id":"p37s2","text":" shared mode uses the profile's `runtimeMode` field; resetting it to `null` follows the live `mode` "},{"id":"p37s3","text":"default without erasing other settings."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"## Example"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### Stay inside the original scope"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"### Approve a real direction change"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"The plugin provides a small set of alignment primitives:"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"- `establish_baseline` records the current goal, explicit constraints, must-preserve behavior, allow"},{"id":"p45s2","text":"ed scope and settled user decisions;
- `report_drift` surfaces a material direction change, asks thr"},{"id":"p45s3","text":"ough DSH's native user-question path and records the exact decision;
- `/align` reports current alig"},{"id":"p45s4","text":"nment status and requests a fresh inspection;
- `/align-mode` changes Auto / Manual / Off behavior w"},{"id":"p45s5","text":"ithout requiring you to uninstall the plugin."},{"id":"p46s1","text":"Canonical alignment state is kept in durable sidecar storage instead of being mixed into normal DSH "},{"id":"p46s2","text":"session events. That keeps resume/fork/compaction behavior stable and avoids turning the session log"},{"id":"p46s3","text":" into a plugin-specific state database."},{"id":"p47s1","text":"## Runtime mode model"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"Effective mode follows this order:"},{"id":"p49s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p50s1","text":"This means two live sessions can use different alignment modes without leaking state into each other"},{"id":"p50s2","text":"his means two live sessions can use different alignment modes without leaking state into each other."},{"id":"p51s1","text":"Switching modes changes which alignment capabilities are active. It does **not** delete the requirem"},{"id":"p51s2","text":"ent baseline or drift history."},{"id":"p52s1","text":"## Web UI"},{"id":"p53s1","text":"In supported DSH Web builds, the plugin includes a small floating alignment control that exposes the"},{"id":"p53s2","text":" current session mode and shared mode without requiring manual profile edits."},{"id":"p54s1","text":"The UI and `/align-mode` operate on the same underlying state, so they are intended to stay consiste"},{"id":"p54s2","text":"nt. Live browser interaction was not verified for this release candidate; the packed CLI/Web HTTP pa"},{"id":"p54s3","text":"e browser interaction was not verified for this release candidate; the packed CLI/Web HTTP path was."},{"id":"p55s1","text":"## Long-running tasks can wait and continue"},{"id":"p56s1","text":"When the agent genuinely needs your decision, the expected behavior is to wait instead of guessing."},{"id":"p57s1","text":"The same design principle applies to requirement drift: pause for the high-impact choice, record it,"},{"id":"p57s2","text":" then continue from the new baseline."},{"id":"p58s1","text":"## What this plugin does not do"},{"id":"p59s1","text":"- It does **not** replace DSH Plan Mode.
- It does **not** turn every engineering choice into a user"},{"id":"p59s2","text":" question.
- It does **not** require a full PRD or spec before work can start.
- It does **not** rew"},{"id":"p59s3","text":"rite DSH core packages.
- It does **not** continuously interrupt clear tasks.
- It does **not** dele"},{"id":"p59s4","text":"te alignment state when modes change."},{"id":"p60s1","text":"## Uninstall"},{"id":"p61s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p62s1","text":"`Off` is not the same as uninstalling: Off keeps the plugin installed so the session can switch back"},{"id":"p62s2","text":" to Auto or Manual at runtime."}],"truncated":true}
